From a3540ecadceca4d771668b01d37837b7787685c4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The browser Authors <noreply@browser.invalid>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 17:38:19 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 11/61] input-actions

The Input domain's actions that move like a hand: dispatchKeystrokes and
dispatchMousePath (with outcomes, read-back and typo rules), revealElement,
moveTo, scrollBy, selectOptions, fillDateTime, pickColor, chooseFiles,
performDrag, dispatchKeyChord, dispatchPaste and probeMovementPersona; the
sigma-lognormal path planner, the move/scroll/drag/select/temporal/color/
file sessions, the action-outcome watch (navigations, new tabs, refused
popups, prints), synthetic-event fidelity (real screen coordinates, lock
keys, wheel ticks) and a timer-driven gesture clock.

Typed text has one person's rhythm: each key is timed from the key
before it, by a gap that depends on the two keys, and is held for a time
of its own, so a quick typist has the next key down before the last is
up; Shift is a key of its own, and a Shift held alone repeats; one
identity is one typist, drawn from the persona seed; and every key event
waits for the keyboard's next report (every 8 ms) and is stamped as it
goes. The tables are in keyboard_typing_tables.inc: without the private
layer's measured block it types as a plain typist.

Riders in files this commit owns: Input.pdl carries the
permissionPromptDismissed event (dismiss-permission-prompts);
content/browser/BUILD.gn lists the agent-snapshot and frame-stream
sources and video-recording's (the recorder and its loopback of a tab's
sound, and the encoding service's mojom as a dependency);
protocol_config.json registers the Page agent and frame-stream
commands, video-recording's Browser commands and its Page command
agentMarkSecretField; input_handler.cc holds the per-tab cursor lookup
(cursor-overlay) and the private-clipboard check (dispatchPaste). In a
Linux build presenting Windows the three Windows-only behaviours take
Windows' form: NumLock on in the lock-key state, wheel notches reported
as notches, and CRLF line breaks in a paste.
