+// Input.performDrag's executor: one drag carried out whole from what the
+// page says, and answered once. It surveys the page before anything is
+// pressed and refuses there when the drag cannot be done; then it moves the
+// hand to the grab, presses, tells a native drag from a pointer one by what
+// the first leg starts, turns the wheel under the hand where the target must
+// be scrolled to, lands, checks the pointer is over the target, rests, lets
+// go and reads what changed.
+//
+// The owner's rules, and how each holds by construction:
+//  (a) The last wheel notch comes before the last movement. A notch is
+//      turned only in the carry phase (Spin and SendNotch refuse any other),
+//      and the approach starts only from a carry reading taken once the last
+//      spin's scroll has settled -- by the watch's frames -- or before any
+//      notch at all. A re-plan waits out a notch still in flight, and a frame
+//      showing the scrolled box still, before it reads the page again.
+//  (b) The pointer is verified over the target before the button comes up.
+//      The let-go runs only from a verify that passed: for an element, a hit
+//      check at the landing (native) or the landing inside the target's slot
+//      (pointer); and at the let-go itself nothing watched has scrolled since
+//      the landing was read, and, native, the landing is still inside the
+//      target, the page has answered the last dragover and taken it, and a
+//      second hit check at the very pixel the last dragover used reaches the
+//      target. Anything else is a correction.
+// Autoscroll bands: the page is surveyed again at every stage, before every
+// approach and after every settle, so every leg is planned on the band map
+// as it is (DragTerrain::Constraints): a run of points in one box's band
+// takes at most 70 ms, its exit included. Legs end only at calm points: a
+// wheel station inside its calm region, a calm landing, the calm point
+// beside an in-band landing, each checked with Blink's own band walk on
+// arrival (native). An in-band landing is verified from that calm point and
+// reached by a dart whose 1-99 % span is 80 ms; the rest, the last checks
+// and the drop (its wait for the page's answers capped) take what is left of
+// 110 ms. A guard (native drags, from the dragovers sent) darts out of a
+// band the hand has been in for 140 ms and makes the plan again.
+
